 "parsed": {
  "reachable": false,
  "rationale": "Only mfa_admin and mfa_dbadmin are deployed, so every patched_* constant, segmented and mfa_user are false. The attacker can get far: exploit_web gives foothold_web, pivot_internal gives reach_internal (no segmentation), and steal_user_cred gives stolen_user. auth_appserver, auth_apiserver and auth_ciserver then work because mfa_user is false. Kerberoasting yields stolen_admin, and escalate_ciserver followed by leak_secrets_ciserver yields stolen_dbadmin. However, mfa_admin blocks auth_dc and auth_adfs, so foothold_dc, foothold_adfs, admin_dc and admin_adfs can never be reached. auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup each require (NOT mfa_dbadmin OR admin_dc OR admin_adfs), and all three of those are false. These auth techniques are the only way to get footholds on db, fileserver or backup. Without a foothold there is no admin on those hosts, so none of the exfiltrate_* techniques can fire and exfiltrated stays false."
 },
